___ talking even after everyone had stopped listening. (folytatja \/ nem \u00e1ll meg)<\/p><p>He ________ ________ to become one of the most successful players of his generation. (azut\u00e1n \/ k\u00e9s\u0151bb)<\/p><p>What ________ ________ at the meeting while I was away? (t\u00f6rt\u00e9nt \/ zajlott)<\/p><p>The concert ________ ________ for three hours without a break. (tartott \/ folytat\u00f3dott)<\/p><p>folytatja \/ nem \u00e1ll meg \/ azut\u00e1n \/ t\u00f6rt\u00e9nt \/ tartott<\/p><p>Negative meaning (HU): abbahagyja \/ meg\u00e1ll \/ v\u00e9get \u00e9r<\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ ________ doing sth = folytatja a cselekv\u00e9st (go on ig\u00e9b\u0151l)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ ________ to do sth = azut\u00e1n valami m\u00e1st csin\u00e1l \/ tov\u00e1bbl\u00e9p<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 what ________ ________ ? = mi t\u00f6rt\u00e9nt? \/ mi zajlott?<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ ________ for + id\u0151 = addig tartott \/ ennyi ideig folyt<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 it ________ ________ like this = \u00edgy ment ez tov\u00e1bb \/ \u00edgy folytat\u00f3dott<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p>phrasal verb: go on (past: went on)<\/p><p>past tense \/ -ing form: went on \/ going on<\/p><p>common pair: go on talking \/ go on to do \/ what&#039;s going on \/ go on for hours \/ life goes on<\/p><p>similar: continue \/ carry on \/ proceed \/ happen \/ last<\/p><p>negative: stop \/ give up \/ end \/ come to a halt<\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":null,"review":{"state":"review","interval":4,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"5 nap","good":"10 nap","easy":"13 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-06T21:11:07+00:00"},{"id":51203,"front":"<p>She ________drew some cash from the ATM before heading to the market. (kivesz \/ felvesz)<\/p><p>The army was ordered to ________ from the region immediately. (visszavonul \/ kivonul)<\/p><p>He ________drew his complaint after the issue was resolved. (visszavon \/ visszasz\u00edv)<\/p><p>She began to ________ from her friends after the difficult breakup. (visszah\u00faz\u00f3dik \/ elszigetel\u0151dik)<\/p><p>kivesz \/ visszavon \/ visszavonul \/ visszah\u00faz\u00f3dik<\/p><p>Negative meaning (HU): befizet \/ el\u0151re nyomul \/ fenntart \/ kitart<\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ money = p\u00e9nzt vesz ki (bankb\u00f3l)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ from sth = visszavonul \/ kil\u00e9p valamib\u0151l<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ________ a statement \/ complaint = visszavon egy kijelent\u00e9st \/ panaszt<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 f\u0151n\u00e9v: ________al = kivon\u00e1s \/ visszavon\u00e1s \/ elvon\u00e1s (drogt\u00f3l)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 szab\u00e1lytalan ige: ________ \u2192 withdrew \u2192 withdrawn<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p>verb: withdraw (irregular)<\/p><p>past tense \/ past participle: withdrew \/ withdrawn<\/p><p>noun: withdrawal<\/p><p>common pair: withdraw money \/ withdraw from \/ withdraw a statement \/ withdrawal symptoms<\/p><p>similar: retreat \/ pull out \/ take back \/ remove \/ step back<\/p><p>negative: deposit \/ advance \/ maintain \/ commit<\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":null,"review":{"state":"review","interval":2,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"3 nap","good":"5 nap","easy":"7 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-06T20:59:40+00:00"},{"id":51255,"front":"<p>The children&#039;s faces were full of _______ when they saw the presents. <em>(\u00f6r\u00f6m \/ lelkesed\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>It was a _______ to the organizers that the event ran so smoothly. <em>(megtiszteltet\u00e9s \/ \u00f6r\u00f6mteli dolog)<\/em><\/p><p>The research findings provided a significant _______ to the field of neuroscience. <em>(hozz\u00e1j\u00e1rul\u00e1s \/ fejl\u0151d\u00e9s)<\/em><